,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272186015,"data":"--- [algebra.functions.grid_coloring] ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272187212,"data":"Triggers: function on NxN grid, consecutive triple constraint, modular coloring\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272188989,"data":"Technique: The problem asks for the 100th smallest value of g(4000,4036) where g satisfies an L-shaped consecutive-triple condition. The trap is assuming ALL non-negative integers are achievable (giving 99). The key insight is that the residues mod 3 force only multiples of 3 when x === y (mod 3), yielding answer N.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272199623,"data":"Question: There is a function \\( g: \\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N} \\) such that \\( g(0,0) = 0 \\), and for any \\(x, y \\in \\mathbb{N}\\), there exists \\(n \\in \\mathbb{N}\\) such that the set \\(\\{g(x,y), g(x,y+1), g(x+1,y)\\}\\) equals \\(\\{n, n+1, n+2\\}\\). Find the 100th smallest possible value of \\(g(4000, 4036)\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272203259,"data":"Answer: First observe that the condition {g(x,y), g(x,y+1), g(x+1,y)} = {n, n+1, n+2} means the three values are consecutive, so modulo 3 they form a permutation of {0,1,2}. This forces g to be a proper 3-coloring of the grid under horizontal/vertical adjacency. Two explicit solutions g1(x,y) = x+2y and g2(x,y) = 2x+y both satisfy the condition, giving residues x-y and y-x (mod 3) respectively. When x === y (mod 3) (as with 4000 and 4036, since both are === 1 mod 3), only residue 0 is possible, so all values of g(x,y) must be multiples of 3. The maximum achievable value is 3*min(x,y) + 2*|x-y| = 3*4000 + 2*36 = 12072, and all multiples of 3 from 0 to 12072 are achievable (4025 values total). The wrong answer 99 comes from ignoring the mod-3 restriction and assuming all non-negative integers up to some bound are possible. The 100th smallest value is 3*(100-1) = 3*99 = N.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272206604,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272207748,"data":"[END EXPERT NOTES]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":467.272208943,"data":"\n"}
