,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584309364,"data":"Schema: id, category, topic, subtopic, taxonomy, triggers, technique, question, answer\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584310755,"data":"db.execute(\"SELECT taxonomy, triggers, technique FROM problems WHERE category=?\", (CATEGORY,)).fetchall()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584312277,"data":"Find the closest match, then read the full approach:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584313657,"data":"db.execute(\"SELECT technique, question, answer FROM problems WHERE taxonomy=?\", (TAX,)).fetchone()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58431501,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584324512,"data":"Bob has a convex 735-gon in the plane and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584326008,"data":"wishes to construct the centroid of its vertices. He has no standard ruler or compass, but\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584327311,"data":"he does have a device with which he can dissect the segment between two given points\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584328615,"data":"into m equal parts. For how many \\(m \\in [9, 81256]\\) can Bob necessarily accomplish his task? You have access to `math`, `numpy`, and `sympy` for:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584330336,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58433339,"data":"# Symbolic Computation (sympy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584334789,"data":"- Algebraic manipulation and simplification\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584336016,"data":"- Solving equations and systems of equations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584337286,"data":"- Symbolic differentiation and integration\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584338506,"data":"- Number theory functions (primes, divisors, modular arithmetic)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584339735,"data":"- Polynomial operations and factorization\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584340906,"data":"- Working with mathematical expressions symbolically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584342183,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584343225,"data":"# Numerical Computation (numpy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584344471,"data":"- Array operations and linear algebra\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584345606,"data":"- Efficient numerical calculations for large datasets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584346928,"data":"- Matrix operations and eigenvalue problems\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.5843481,"data":"- Statistical computations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584349266,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584350332,"data":"# Mathematical Functions (math):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58435163,"data":"- Standard mathematical functions (trig, log, exp)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584352808,"data":"- Constants like pi and e\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58435404,"data":"- Basic operations for single values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584355224,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584356319,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58435748,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584358716,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584359958,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58436117,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58436255,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584363807,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.5843655,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58436657,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58436771,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584371416,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584372892,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584374226,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584375553,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584376854,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584378145,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584379468,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584381394,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584383173,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584385025,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584386086,"data":"# Library Availability:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584387574,"data":"NOT installed (do NOT import — they WILL fail): pulp, ortools, z3-solver, mip, pyscipopt, pysat, cvxpy, constraint, matplotlib, sklearn.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584389182,"data":"Do not waste turns trying these libraries or probing with try/except.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584390434,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584391508,"data":"Available and recommended:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58439266,"data":"- sympy, numpy, scipy, networkx, mpmath, math, itertools, functools, fractions, collections, decimal, heapq, random, statistics\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584393994,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584395348,"data":"Replacements for unavailable optimization/constraint libraries:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584396692,"data":"- Integer/Binary Linear Programming (replaces pulp, mip, ortools):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584398389,"data":"  from scipy.optimize import milp, LinearConstraint, Bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584399808,"data":"  import numpy as np\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584400944,"data":"  res = milp(c=c_vec, constraints=LinearConstraint(A, lb, ub),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584402184,"data":"             integrality=np.ones(n), bounds=Bounds(0, 1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584403369,"data":"  # res.success, res.x (solution vector), res.fun (objective value)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.5844046,"data":"- Linear Programming: scipy.optimize.linprog(c, A_ub=A, b_ub=b, method=\"highs\")\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584405947,"data":"- Assignment problems: scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment(cost_matrix)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584407389,"data":"- Graph algorithms (matching, shortest path, components): import networkx as nx\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.58440862,"data":"- Constraint satisfaction: encode as ILP via scipy.optimize.milp, or backtracking with pruning\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584411991,"data":"- Number theory: sympy.ntheory or random (Monte Carlo verification)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584413236,"data":"- Geometry: fractions (exact rational) + sympy, avoid floating point\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584414491,"data":"- Game theory/DP: functools.lru_cache for memoized recursion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584415748,"data":"=== END USER PROMPT ===\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":936.584417064,"data":"\n"}
